# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps secrets and
# patient data out of the image. Anything listed here is never sent to the
# Docker daemon at all.

# ── Must never enter an image ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Every .env on this machine: clinic DATABASE_URLs, JWT secrets, API keys.
# An image is pushed to a registry, so a secret baked into one is a
# published secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.mcp.json

# Patient files: scans, X-rays, lab reports. 22 MB of real PHI locally.
uploads/
**/uploads/

# ── Rebuilt inside the image ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
**/src/generated
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Irrelevant to the APIs ────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.github
.vercel
**/.vercel
apps/clinic-web/dist
apps/provider-console/dist

# The unrelated apps' SOURCE is excluded, but not their package.json --
# npm ci resolves every workspace member against the lockfile and fails
# if one named there is missing, so the manifests have to reach the build.
apps/mobile/**
!apps/mobile/package.json
apps/business-dashboard/**
!apps/business-dashboard/package.json
apps/admin/**
!apps/admin/package.json
apps/api/**
!apps/api/package.json

# ── Noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode
.idea
coverage
*.tar.gz
*.dump
docs
